[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Purging CSS and Tree Shaking Unused Styles in Bootstrap"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap is a powerful and comprehensive CSS framework, but it comes with a significant file size drawback. When you include the entire compiled Bootstrap library, you are shipping thousands of rules for components like modals, carousels, and accordions that your project may never actually use. Purging CSS and utilizing tree shaking allow you to strip away these unused styles, drastically reducing your CSS bundle size for faster load times."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Why Purge CSS with Bootstrap?"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"A standard production build of Bootstrap 5 can easily exceed 200KB uncompressed. However, a typical website only utilizes a small fraction of these classes. By scanning your HTML, JavaScript, and template files, CSS purgers identify exactly which classes are used and discard the rest. This technique frequently reduces Bootstrap's CSS footprint by 80% to 90%."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"To implement CSS purging effectively, you should ideally use Bootstrap via Sass rather than the precompiled CSS files. This gives build tools full visibility into the source variables and mixins."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"npm install bootstrap @fullhuman/postcss-purgecss postcss --save-dev"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Configuring PostCSS PurgeCSS"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Create a configuration file named postcss.config.js in the root of your project. This file will instruct PostCSS on how to find your template files and which classes to safely ignore during the purge process."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    require('autoprefixer'),
    require('@fullhuman/postcss-purgecss')({
      content: ['./index.html', './src/**/*.js', './src/**/*.vue'],
      defaultExtractor: content => content.match(/[A-Za-z0-9-_:/]+/g) || [],
      safelist: [/^carousel/, /^modal/, /^dropdown-backdrop/]
    })
  ]
};"},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"content: Specifies the paths to all template and script files where Bootstrap classes might be referenced."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"defaultExtractor: Uses a regular expression to capture valid CSS class names inside your markup files."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"safelist: Prevents dynamic classes added by JavaScript (such as modals or popovers) from being accidentally purged."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Handling Dynamic Classes Safely"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap relies heavily on JavaScript to toggle states using classes like .show, .fade, or .collapsing. If your static HTML analysis does not pick these up, your interactive components may break. Always use the safelist property in your PurgeCSS configuration to preserve these critical utility and state classes."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Tree Shaking Sass Modules"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"Instead of importing all of Bootstrap at once, you can import only the specific modules you need. Create a custom custom.scss file and import components selectively."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"// 1. Include functions, variables, and mixins first
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/functions";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/variables";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/mixins";

// 2. Import only required layout and components
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/root";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/reboot";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/type";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/grid";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/buttons";"},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Combining modular Sass imports with automated PostCSS PurgeCSS ensures your Bootstrap-powered applications remain lightning fast and lightweight. Always test your production builds thoroughly to ensure no dynamic components lost their styling due to aggressive purging."}]
